WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.472 --> 00:00:02.230
(playful instrumental music)

00:00:02.230 --> 00:00:03.100
- [Narrator] This is the town

00:00:03.100 --> 00:00:06.640
of Chippewa Falls, nestled
along the Chippewa River

00:00:06.640 --> 00:00:09.300
in the beautiful Northwoods of Wisconsin.

00:00:09.300 --> 00:00:10.930
It's home to the Leinenkugel family

00:00:10.930 --> 00:00:13.550
and the Jacob Leinenkugel Brewing Company.

00:00:13.550 --> 00:00:15.550
Brewer of Leinenkugel's Summer Shandy

00:00:15.550 --> 00:00:17.933
and one of the oldest
breweries in America.

00:00:18.770 --> 00:00:21.640
So what's it take for one
family to keep the beer flowing

00:00:21.640 --> 00:00:23.839
for over 150 years?

00:00:23.839 --> 00:00:26.900
It's harder than you'd think.

00:00:26.900 --> 00:00:31.130
Our story begins in 1867,
with a young German immigrant,

00:00:31.130 --> 00:00:33.160
a brewer named Jacob Leinenkugel.

00:00:33.160 --> 00:00:35.540
- I like to refer to my
great-great-grandfather

00:00:35.540 --> 00:00:37.238
as No-Neck Leinie.

00:00:37.238 --> 00:00:39.410
- [Narrator] For centuries his
family had been brewing beer

00:00:39.410 --> 00:00:42.930
in Germany, now he was looking
to make his mark in America.

00:00:42.930 --> 00:00:45.340
In Chippewa Falls, Jacob
discovered a source

00:00:45.340 --> 00:00:47.030
of pure spring water.

00:00:47.030 --> 00:00:50.000
- Which makes for a
great lager-style beer.

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:51.430
- [Narrator] He also discovered--

00:00:51.430 --> 00:00:54.223
- Twenty five hundred thirsty lumberjacks.

00:00:54.223 --> 00:00:56.395
- [Narrator] So he built a brewery.

00:00:56.395 --> 00:00:58.340
But brewing was hard work.

00:00:58.340 --> 00:01:00.940
To make ends meet, he enlisted his family.

00:01:00.940 --> 00:01:02.840
- I think the hardest worker
out of that family was probably

00:01:02.840 --> 00:01:03.800
his wife Josephine.

00:01:03.800 --> 00:01:06.290
- My great, great, great grandmother.

00:01:06.290 --> 00:01:08.500
- [Narrator] Every day
she woke up at three a.m.

00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:11.560
to cook four meals for
the 20 brewery workers,

00:01:11.560 --> 00:01:13.810
all while raising four children.

00:01:13.810 --> 00:01:15.480
- Lotta credit goes to Josephine.

00:01:15.480 --> 00:01:16.980
- [Narrator] The little brewery prospered,

00:01:16.980 --> 00:01:19.380
but then Jacob's partner quit,

00:01:19.380 --> 00:01:23.090
and Josephine died of pneumonia, aged 44.

00:01:23.090 --> 00:01:25.740
With a family to support,
Jacob had no choice

00:01:25.740 --> 00:01:28.870
but to keep brewing and the
people of Chippewa Falls

00:01:28.870 --> 00:01:32.693
loved the beer so much they
elected Jacob mayor, twice.

00:01:33.580 --> 00:01:36.580
- They continued to brew great
beer, all the way up until

00:01:36.580 --> 00:01:39.550
the Federal government
put us out of business.

00:01:39.550 --> 00:01:41.700
- [Narrator] In 1920
the United States banned

00:01:41.700 --> 00:01:43.800
the manufacture and sale of alcohol.

00:01:43.800 --> 00:01:46.710
The dark days of prohibition
descended upon America

00:01:46.710 --> 00:01:49.450
and hundreds of breweries vanished.

00:01:49.450 --> 00:01:51.830
- We had stay in business
and we had to stay together

00:01:51.830 --> 00:01:52.683
as a family.

00:01:53.660 --> 00:01:54.880
- [Narrator] To survive prohibition,

00:01:54.880 --> 00:01:56.980
they turned to Jacob's daughter Susan,

00:01:56.980 --> 00:01:59.584
electing her president
just six years after women

00:01:59.584 --> 00:02:01.570
won the right to vote.

00:02:01.570 --> 00:02:03.463
- Third cousin twice removed.

00:02:04.600 --> 00:02:06.850
You have to go back
through a family lineage

00:02:06.850 --> 00:02:08.450
to find that out.

00:02:08.450 --> 00:02:10.740
- [Narrator] She saved
Leinenkugels by brewing

00:02:10.740 --> 00:02:12.550
soda pop and mixers.

00:02:12.550 --> 00:02:15.400
- [Dick] I gotta believe that
the mixers were being mixed

00:02:15.400 --> 00:02:16.773
with something else.

00:02:17.730 --> 00:02:19.700
- [Narrator] When
prohibition came to a close,

00:02:19.700 --> 00:02:21.190
two other Leinenkugel women.

00:02:21.190 --> 00:02:24.210
- [Dick] Katherine
Leinenkugel and Rose Casper--

00:02:24.210 --> 00:02:25.530
- [Narrator] Came to the rescue.

00:02:25.530 --> 00:02:27.690
- [Dick] They actually
mortgaged their homes to get the

00:02:27.690 --> 00:02:30.600
brewing equipment back up and operating.

00:02:30.600 --> 00:02:33.780
- Not a lot of breweries
came out of prohibition.

00:02:33.780 --> 00:02:35.480
Leinenkugels was fortunate.

00:02:35.480 --> 00:02:37.590
- [Narrator] The reinvigorated
brewery was soon joined

00:02:37.590 --> 00:02:40.960
by Bill Leinenkugel, a
Marine returned from war.

00:02:40.960 --> 00:02:43.884
- Bill, my dad, was really
the guy that expanded

00:02:43.884 --> 00:02:47.780
the brewery's footprint into
the Northwoods of Wisconsin.

00:02:47.780 --> 00:02:49.630
- [Narrator] Bill had five
children, and they helped

00:02:49.630 --> 00:02:51.900
out around the brewery
as Bill hit the road,

00:02:51.900 --> 00:02:55.480
spreading the gospel of
Leinenkugels across the Northwoods.

00:02:55.480 --> 00:02:57.920
He just went out and met the people.

00:02:57.920 --> 00:02:59.930
Put a nice cold Leinies in
their hands and they loved

00:02:59.930 --> 00:03:02.400
the guy and that's what they stuck with.

00:03:02.400 --> 00:03:04.720
- [Narrator] Soon, he had
transformed Leinenkugels

00:03:04.720 --> 00:03:06.623
into a major Midwest brewery.

00:03:07.730 --> 00:03:09.430
But it wasn't enough.

00:03:09.430 --> 00:03:11.620
Small brewers were being
priced out of business

00:03:11.620 --> 00:03:14.260
by big brewers who had invaded their turf.

00:03:14.260 --> 00:03:16.650
- Economics 101, folks.

00:03:16.650 --> 00:03:18.260
- [Narrator] Back when
Leinenkugels got started,

00:03:18.260 --> 00:03:21.370
there were nearly 4,000
breweries spread across America.

00:03:21.370 --> 00:03:24.370
By the late 70s, only 89 remained.

00:03:24.370 --> 00:03:26.850
As Leinenkugels became
engulfed in the price wars,

00:03:26.850 --> 00:03:28.230
- Ask for Leinenkugels.

00:03:28.230 --> 00:03:29.443
- [Narrator] It received help from a

00:03:29.443 --> 00:03:30.793
fellow Wisconsin brewery.

00:03:31.935 --> 00:03:35.520
- It was in 1987 that my
dad received a letter from

00:03:35.520 --> 00:03:36.620
Miller Brewing Company.

00:03:36.620 --> 00:03:39.630
My dad says I think they
want us to buy them.

00:03:39.630 --> 00:03:41.863
Well, it was obviously
the other way around.

00:03:43.000 --> 00:03:44.520
- [Narrator] Leinenkugels
kept its family roots,

00:03:44.520 --> 00:03:47.373
and Bill's three sons built
upon their father's legacy.

00:03:48.440 --> 00:03:50.450
- After partnering with
Miller Brewing Company,

00:03:50.450 --> 00:03:53.080
we began to develop
different styles of beers

00:03:53.080 --> 00:03:56.123
that we probably wouldn't have
been able to do on our own.

00:03:58.180 --> 00:04:00.990
- [Mahala] Can you list
all the Leinenkugels beers?

00:04:00.990 --> 00:04:03.410
- There are quite a few,
so you'll have to have

00:04:03.410 --> 00:04:04.660
some more film.

00:04:04.660 --> 00:04:05.710
- Leinenkugel Original.

00:04:05.710 --> 00:04:06.543
- Honey Weiss.

00:04:06.543 --> 00:04:07.376
- Berry Weiss.

00:04:07.376 --> 00:04:08.209
- Canoe Paddler.

00:04:08.209 --> 00:04:09.042
- Sunset Wheat.

00:04:09.042 --> 00:04:09.875
- Creamy Dark.

00:04:09.875 --> 00:04:11.410
- Big Butt Doppelbock.

00:04:11.410 --> 00:04:14.232
- What else? (laughs)

00:04:14.232 --> 00:04:15.940
- Leinenkugel's Summer Shandy.

00:04:16.900 --> 00:04:19.280
- It wasn't until the
development of Leinenkugel's

00:04:19.280 --> 00:04:22.700
Summer Shandy that we
decided to take Leinenkugels

00:04:22.700 --> 00:04:24.440
to the rest of the country.

00:04:24.440 --> 00:04:27.470
- Whether it's the island
of Manhattan, New York

00:04:27.470 --> 00:04:31.000
or all the way up to the
great frontier of Alaska,

00:04:31.000 --> 00:04:32.273
that's pretty cool.

00:04:32.273 --> 00:04:34.214
- Okay everybody, here we go!

00:04:34.214 --> 00:04:37.997
♪ When we're gone from here ♪

00:04:37.997 --> 00:04:41.167
♪ The gang will be
drinkin' all the beer. ♪

00:04:41.167 --> 00:04:44.840
- [Narrator] In 2017
Leinenkugels celebrated 150 years

00:04:44.840 --> 00:04:46.970
as the pride of the Northwoods.

00:04:46.970 --> 00:04:49.170
And with time, comes tradition.

00:04:49.170 --> 00:04:51.110
- Leinenkugels and Chippewa
Falls are synonymous.

00:04:51.110 --> 00:04:51.960
When you see a Leinenkugels,

00:04:51.960 --> 00:04:53.333
you think Chippewa Falls, Wisconsin.

00:04:53.333 --> 00:04:54.890
When you say Chippewa Falls, Wisconsin,

00:04:54.890 --> 00:04:56.240
you think Leinenkugel beer.

00:04:57.400 --> 00:04:59.750
- There's generations of
Leinenkugels that have worked

00:04:59.750 --> 00:05:02.490
here at the brewery, but
there's also been generations

00:05:02.490 --> 00:05:04.718
of other families that have
worked here and continue

00:05:04.718 --> 00:05:06.930
to work here to this day.

00:05:06.930 --> 00:05:09.000
- Our hats off go to them as well.

00:05:09.000 --> 00:05:13.520
It's a legacy that was started
in 1867 and we're gonna

00:05:13.520 --> 00:05:16.443
work really hard to ensure
that that legacy continues.

